{
  "formatVersion": 1,
  "profileId": "vega-49",
  "recordedAt": "2026-09-04",
  "note": "A fixture, and it says so: Nebula Instruments and the Vega 49 do not exist. It is here because a format that has only ever described one device has not been shown to describe a device. Every expectation was derived from the byte layout and the normalisation rules of the specification, never from a run of the decoder -- an expectation taken from the code under test proves only that the code equals itself. Expectations are in the PROFILE's vocabulary, a control id and which of its bindings answered, not in MiniHub's: naming is what the host adds afterwards, and the shared decoder must not know those names.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "dial-one-default",
      "why": "Dial 1 on the play layer, and it is CC 74 -- the same message the MiniLab 3 sends from K1",
      "sourceName": "Vega49 Keys",
      "bytes": [
        176,
        74,
        13
      ],
      "parsed": {
        "type": "cc",
        "channel": 1,
        "controller": 74,
        "value": 13,
        "raw": [
          176,
          74,
          13
        ]
      },
      "expect": {
        "controlId": "dial-one",
        "bindingIndex": 0,
        "normalizedValue": 0.10236220472440945,
        "rawValue": 13
      }
    },
    {
